 "text": "Martin County\nCommunity\nCities\nCommunity Links\nCounty History\nCourthouse History\nParks\nFacilities\nMap\nRules\nBright Lake\nCedar Hanson\nKlessig\nPerch Lake\nTimberlane\nWolter\nSchools\nYour Government\nAdvertisement for Bids\nBoard of Commissioners\nAgendas/Minutes\nDistrict 1\nDistrict 2\nDistrict 3\nDistrict 4\nDistrict 5\nData Practices\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAuditor/Treasurer\nCoordinator\nCounty Attorney\nDrainage Administration\nEconomic Development\nExtension\nHighway\nHuman Resources\nHuman Services\nInformation Technology\nLibrary\nPlanning & Zoning\nProbation\nPublic Transit\nRecorder\nRecycling/Solid Waste\nSheriff\nVeteran Services\nVictim/Witness\nDistrict Court\nLaw Library\nElections\nElection Judges\nPublic Officials Guide\nFee Schedule\nObserved Holidays\nOrdinances\nSalary Compliance\nI Want To\nApply\nProperty Tax Abatement\nFind\nActive Warrants\nJail Roster\nProperty Information\nSafe At Home Info\nPay\nFines\nProperty Taxes\nVote\nContact Us\nTranslate\nSelect your language.\nEnglish\nSpanish\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nmore Languages\nEnglish\nAfrikaans\nAlbanian\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSomali\nSpanish\nSwahili\nSwedish\nTamil\nTelugu\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nUrdu\nVietnamese\nWelsh\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\nServices!\nForms!\nAll Of Martin!\nServices!\nForms!\nAll Of Martin!\nslide 1 of 1\nRecorder\nHome\nYour Government\nDepartments\nRecorder\nSub Menu\nPage Menu\nRecorder Home\nBirth\nDeath\nGenealogy Research\nHonor Rewards\nMarriage\nNotary\nPassports\nReal Estate\nTax Liens\nThe Martin County Recorder is the custodian of all records pertaining to real estate, subdivision plats, state and federal tax liens, vital records (birth, death, marriage), ministerial credentials, notary public commissions, and military discharges. The records are permanently preserved in an archival quality format and are made accessible to the public.\nDisclaimer: By law, staff at the county recorder’s office cannot give legal advice, interpret laws,\nor assist with the preparation of legal documents. We are only permitted to provide\ngeneral information about filing procedures, recording requirements, and publicly\navailable resources. If you need assistance with legal questions, interpreting\ndocuments, or determining how to proceed, we strongly encourage you to consult a\nlicensed attorney. There may also be a law library or referral service available for\nfurther research or to help you find legal counsel\nMain Phone Line: 507-238-3213\nMartin County Recorder\nMichelle Duncan\n507-238-3255\nmichelle.duncan@martincountymn.gov\nDeputy Recorders:\nSarah Halvorson\n507-238-3254\nsarah.halvorson@martincountymn.gov\nJami Poulson\n507-238-3202\njami.poulson@martincountymn.gov\nServices:\nRecord real estate documents\nVital Records (birth, death, and marriage records)\nIssue marriage licenses\nFile Ordain/Officiant Credentials\nPassport Acceptance Agent\nPassport Photos\nFile and obtain military discharges\nIf the military release is yours and it was recorded in Martin County after your discharge, you may obtain a copy. Federal regulations and data privacy rules require that military separations be available only to the veteran or those with a tangible interest (spouse, family member, etc.). The documents are free to residents with tangible interest.\nFile state and federal tax liens\nFile Notary Public commissions\nNotary Fraud Alert\nProperty Fraud Alert\nHonor Rewards Program\nShare this page\nShare this page\n-->\nClose\nContact Us!\n201 Lake Avenue Fairmont, MN 56031\n507-238-3124\nOpen 8:00 am - 5:00 pm, M - F\nContact Us\nQuicklinks!\nAgendas & Minutes\nDocument Center\nJail Roster\nEmployment Opportunities\nPublic Notices\nProperty Search\nPublic Officials Guide\nCommissioner Login\nCounty Email\nEmployee Login\nPowered by revize., the Government Website Experts | Login\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nClose Read More",
